  "use_case": "Railroad freight demand forecasting and lane optimization",
  "space_title": "FreightSight Analytics - Freight Demand Forecasting 📈",
  "space_description": "**Scenario:** You run freight demand and lane economics for FreightSight Analytics, a Class I railroad moving carloads across 20 lanes from PRB coal to Chicago-LA intermodal. Your forecast models are drifting on a few commodities, and lanes flagged as Growing demand are running utilization above 90% while your pricing discipline varies wildly by commodity. Which lanes should you commit more capacity to, and which commodities are quietly eroding your forecast accuracy and revenue?\n\n**Questions:**\n\n1. Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset (agent)\n2. What is my current carload volume and freight revenue by commodity and origin region? (agent)\n3. Which lanes are flagged as Growing demand with utilization above 90%, and what is their forecasted revenue versus their current average forecast error? (agent)",
