  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports Freight Demand Forecasting and Lane Optimization for a Class I railroad operating 20 lanes across Intermodal, Coal, Chemicals, Agricultural, Automotive, Metals, Forest Products, and General merchandise. Stakeholders include the VP Sales & Marketing (carloads, revenue, rate per car, demand trend), Network Planning (utilization, transit days, capacity by lane), and the CFO (forecast accuracy / MAPE, forecasted revenue, commodity-mix risk).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Total carloads = SUM(carloads); primary volume metric across bulk + intermodal\n- Freight revenue = SUM(revenue_usd); top-line\n- Revenue per carload = revenue_usd / NULLIF(carloads, 0); yield indicator\n- Average rate per car = AVG(avg_rate_per_car); pricing discipline by commodity\n- Lane utilization = AVG(utilization_pct); healthy ~75-90%; >95% signals capacity constraint\n- Delayed share = delayed_count / shipment_count; service reliability\n- Forecast accuracy (MAPE) = AVG(forecast_error_pct); world-class rail forecasting models hit 3-5%; <10% is acceptable; >15% triggers model review\n- Forecast bias = forecasted_carloads - actual_carloads; positive = over-forecasting, negative = under-forecasting\n- Demand patterns: Intermodal peaks Sep-Nov (peak-shipping), Agricultural peaks Sep-Nov (harvest), Coal peaks Dec-Feb (heating), Chemicals peaks Apr-Jun\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - freight_kpi_monthly (source: shipping_lanes) — dims: shipment_date, commodity, origin_region, shipment_status; measures: total_carloads, total_revenue, avg_transit_days, shipment_count, delayed_count, unique_lane_count, max_carloads.\n  - forecast_kpi_monthly (source: demand_forecasts) — dims: forecast_month, commodity, origin_region, model_version; measures: total_forecasted_carloads, total_actual_carloads, avg_forecast_error, total_forecasted_revenue, forecast_count, unique_lane_count, max_forecasted_carloads.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. lane_id, lane_name, avg_rate_per_car, utilization_pct, demand_trend, forecast_error_pct).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset",
    "What is my current carload volume and freight revenue by commodity and origin region?",
    "Which lanes are flagged as Growing demand with utilization above 90%, and what is their forecasted revenue versus their current average forecast error?"
  ],
  "example_sqls": [
    {
      "question": "How many distinct transactions appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', shipment_date) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT transaction) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.shipping_lanes",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has highest carloads changed over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT shipment_date, MEASURE(max_carloads) AS max_carloads",
        "FROM {fqn}.freight_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY shipment_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What has been the peak forecasted carloads each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, MEASURE(max_forecasted_carloads) AS max_forecasted_carloads",
        "FROM {fqn}.forecast_kpi_monthly",
        "GROUP BY ALL",
        "ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How many distinct forecasts appeared each month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT DATE_TRUNC('month', forecast_month) AS month, COUNT(DISTINCT forecast) AS distinct_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_forecasts",
        "GROUP BY 1",
        "ORDER BY 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "Which lanes have the highest total *?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT lane_name, SUM(*) AS record_count, SUM(carloads) AS total_carloads",
        "FROM {fqn}.shipping_lanes",
        "WHERE shipment_status = 'Delayed'",
        "GROUP BY lane_name",
        "ORDER BY total_carloads DESC",
        "LIMIT 10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "What is the trend of total number of bookings over time?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT snapshot_date, SUM(bookings_count) AS total_bookings_count",
        "FROM {fqn}.freight_orders",
        "GROUP BY snapshot_date ORDER BY snapshot_date"
      ]
    },
    {
      "question": "How has average absolute forecast error percentage trended by month?",
      "sql_lines": [
        "SELECT forecast_month, AVG(forecast_error_pct) AS avg_forecast_error_pct",
        "FROM {fqn}.demand_forecasts",
        "GROUP BY forecast_month",
        "ORDER BY forecast_month"
      ]
    }
  ],
